                <invention-title lang="de">LEISTUNGSREGELUNG FÜR WIEDERHOLTE UPLINK-ÜBERTRAGUNGEN</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">COMMANDE DE PUISSANCE POUR TRANSMISSIONS EN LIAISON MONTANTE RÉPÉTÉES</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">POWER CONTROL FOR REPEATED UPLINK TRANSMISSIONS</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>Methods, systems, and devices for wireless communications are described. A method for wireless communication comprises: receiving (905) an uplink grant that schedules a transmission of a physical uplink shared channel, PUSCH, for transmitting uplink data that is associated with a repetition type, wherein the uplink grant indicates a first number of symbols scheduled by the uplink grant for the transmission of the PUSCH; determining (915) a transmission power for transmitting the uplink data based at least in part on the first number of symbols; and transmitting (920) the uplink data in an actual transmission of the PUSCH using the determined transmission power, wherein the actual transmission comprises a second number of symbols and wherein the second number of symbols is different from the first number of symbols.</p>
            </abstract>
